infiltrator-calc (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the Windows GTK/MSYS2 shell with a native Win32 interface over the shared C++ core.
  * Build Windows with Visual Studio/MSVC and the static runtime so the published EXE is standalone.
  * Remove the GTK/GLib portable runtime archive from Windows release assets.
  * Reject Windows builds that import GTK/GLib, GCC, libstdc++, winpthread or VC redistributable DLLs.
  * Keep the Linux GTK4 and iPhone SwiftUI shells on Infiltratr Common 1.18.1.
  * Restore a compact Linux GTK desktop density so the complete keypad fits normal work areas.
  * Reduce Linux keypad height/spacing and disable vertical row stretching so the equals key remains visible.
  * Add a CI regression guard for the Linux desktop size contract.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:40:00 +1000

